  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="work" n="140">
        <pb n="185"/>
        <head>Another.</head>
        <head>140. — ii — VIII. — <quote>It hath been strengthened and I cannot</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="1">Which point to admire the more (<foreign xml:lang="grc">μᾶλλον</foreign>) among the things that<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> befell at the martyrdom of the [illustrious <persName>Romanus</persName> I am<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/> in doubt; at the lawful freedom of speech (<foreign xml:lang="grc">παῤῥησία</foreign>) before his tongue was cut out, or at the speaking without a tongue after [it had been cut out<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/>. In both of them I praise <persName>Christ</persName>, who said beforehand to the combatants (<foreign xml:lang="grc">ἀθληταί</foreign>) of godliness, <quote>Ye <pb n="186"/> shall not consider at all how or what ye shall speak; for it is not ye that speak, but it is the Spirit of your Father that speaketh in you</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/>. By whose prayers, Lord of all, do thou confirm our heart<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/> also that is paralyzed by sin and have mercy upon us, according to the abundance of thy great mercy.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 185, n. 5</orig></choice> Ps. cxxxviii, 6.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 185, n. 6</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>in</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 185, n. 7</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>R. praised by all being</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 185, n. 8</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>the excision</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 186, n. 1</orig></choice> Matth. x, 17-22 <quote>Beware..... And they shall bring you before kings and governors for my sake..... Ye shall speak. It shall be given you..... and children shall rise against their fathers..... shall live</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 186, n. 2</orig></choice> Sir. ii, 12, 13 LXX <quote>Woe to the doubting hearts and to the relaxed hands, and to the sinner that rideth two ways! Woe to the paralyzed heart because it believeth not!</quote></note>
      </noteGrp>
    </body>
